
                    ZAmiNet v1.0 (c) Nick Loman 1995
                   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

ZAmiNet is a file area converter and a file catalogue uploader for the AmiNet
series of CD-ROM's. It may also work with other CD-ROM catalogues, as long
as the Files.BBS format is the same.

Usage
~~~~~

ZAmiNet AREAS/A/S,FILES/A/S,DIR,STARTNO/N,HEADER,CDPATH,RANGE

Converting File Areas
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Example Command Line:

ZAmiNet AREAS DIR DirList.Txt STARTNO 200 HEADER "AmiNet4 CD" CDPATH "CD0:AmiNet/"

After this program has finished, run "UpdateConfigs FILE" for the changes
to take effect.

"DirList.Txt" takes the form of "file directory per line". See included
AmiNet4 CD file.

STARTNO is the file number to start converting the file bases at, in this 
example "biz/dbase" would be area 200 and "util/wb" would be area 324.

HEADER is a string (use quotes) to precede the path name in the area
name. Therefore "AmiNet4 CD [comm/wb]" could be an example name.

CDPATH is the path with postfixing slash or colon to the file areas, e.g.
"CD0:AmiNet/"

Uploading Files
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Example Command Line:

ZAmiNet FILES RANGE "200-324"

This will upload all the files from the Files.BBS file in each file area's
path. The filename, filesize and description will be taken, and the CD
must be in the drive when uploading.

RANGE may have the usual "34,45,67-100,102" parameters.

Turn off File Noting in the General File Configuration program, as you
can't write File Notes to Read only drives!

Caution: This function _will_ take a long time if uploading all the areas!

